WEBVTT

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:04.940
Chieri's in ninth place.

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:07.720
Keep in mind that the early results are simply the current standings.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:10.910
There's no telling how they will change.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:19.080
That's uper-say!

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.280
An understudy in ninth place!

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.140
U-Um, I—

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:23.140
Chieri.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:24.710
It's fine to celebrate.

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:28.760
It's not often that an understudy ranks for the early results.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:30.960
Let's both keep it up.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.680
Oh? Our resident top
contender isn't even ruffled.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:38.830
Second place...

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:43.890
Still frustrated, huh?

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:48.810
Second place is plenty impressive, but that's not enough for her.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.650
"I'll definitely become a successor."

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:55.750
I saw your poster, Chan-Chie.

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:59.020
If that's what you want, why do you look so glum?

00:00:59.020 --> 00:00:59.830
I just...

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:01.780
Aren't you happy?

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:04.470
Then you'll look even more radiant on film!

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.290
That's right! Shine for me!

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:12.380
Yes, yes! That's it! That's it!

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:22.520
Whoops...

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:33.820
A wind that heeds no master now blows.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:37.990
Behold, light shines down through the clouds.

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:44.330
Wanderers strain their ears to hear

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:49.350
and find the power to follow their own paths.

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:55.640
Before me, a hill stretches despairingly high.

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:59.960
But if there's to be a future for me,

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:03.470
I cannot turn my back.

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:06.890
My friend, do you remember?

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:10.480
Here, where we exchanged vows that day,

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:14.950
flowers are blooming in season.

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:19.200
A voice that heeds no master calls.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.430
Behold, the sun has returned,

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:26.160
gradually stripping the land

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.960
of the shadows that had gathered.

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:32.170
Heedless of any master, now is the time.

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:36.470
Yes, we shall set off on our way.

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:42.640
All of us are frail creatures

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:45.700
seeking the shadow of love

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:49.130
and pushing ever onwards.

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:02.240
This handshake event is in anticipation of the Elections.

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:03.910
The fans are more energetic than ever.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.200
Don't let them down now.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.040
Got it!

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:11.000
I'm getting nervous.

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:18.180
They say that the handshaking prior to the Elections has a major effect on the ballots.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:19.990
I didn't need to hear that!

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:21.380
There, there.

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:23.690
Relax, relax!

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:28.020
The Elections are like a festival.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:29.390
If you don't enjoy them, you're missing out!

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:31.300
Kojiharu-san.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.770
That's true.

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:35.320
I voted for you!

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:39.280
You're not supposed to vote for other members though.

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:41.650
But thanks, Megu.

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:42.530
Your support means
the world to me.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:44.230
Sae!

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:53.340
Chieri?

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:54.420
Girls.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:55.380
I forgot to mention something.

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:58.500
The 77th generation will be in the individual lanes this time.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:03:59.880
I-Individual lanes?

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:00.520
Huh?

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:04.520
But all of us together don't have as many fans as a single successor!

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:06.100
That won't be an issue.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:09.360
Those lines!

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:11.050
This is the line for Makoto.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:11.810
This is for Nagisa.

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:14.810
<i>That</i> many people showed up for me?!

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:22.020
It's thanks to our recent renewal
effort and the understudy concert.

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:25.160
Lookit the size of that line over there!

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:27.160
Chieri, that's the line for you.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.820
Holy cow!

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:30.660
That's the sort of turnout you'd get for a successor!

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.620
<i>What's this feeling?</i>

00:04:34.030 --> 00:04:37.130
<i>I felt a twinge right here.</i>

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:39.090
Nagisa-chan!

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:41.780
It's me! Do you remember me?

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:45.050
I-I'm so sorry!

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:47.530
Were you from the last handshake event...?

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:49.140
I'm just kidding!

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:50.480
This is my first time.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:53.840
But I'm already set on supporting you!

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:55.940
I'll help you get elected for sure!

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:57.200
You can count on me!

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:00.020
All right, keep it moving.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:03.320
Be sure to remember me for next time!

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:06.000
Y-You're just as cute in person, Nagisa-san!

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.500
G-Gosh... Thank you.

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:11.210
I'll do my best to help you in the elections!

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.320
You'll do your best?

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:13.500
All right, keep it moving.

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:15.280
Excuse me.

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:18.700
Why would you do that for me?

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:23.670
Because you're doing your best too!

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:28.220
Chieri! The AKB trial sent chills down my spine!

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:30.100
Th-Thank you.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:31.600
But that was just...

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:34.880
If anyone's going to be 00's next pioneer, it'll be you!

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:35.980
Really...?

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:38.580
And the I Girl Noodle commercial they aired last night!

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:40.080
It was awe-inspiring!

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:43.190
I Girl Noodle... commercial?

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:45.400
Thank you.

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:46.950
Chieri! What's wrong?

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:48.700
Chieri?

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:51.880
Even waiting our turn is nerve-wracking.

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:52.660
Yeah.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:56.560
But out of all the things we do,
I like handshaking events the most.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:58.480
You've sure changed.

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:01.170
Not long ago, you were scared out of your wits by the haters.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:03.540
Gosh, Yuuka, stop teasing me about that.

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:04.670
Ribbit, ribbit!

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:07.050
S-Sonata?!

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:09.340
It's hand-shakey practice!

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:12.180
Isn't that butt-gropey?

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:14.640
Chieri.

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:17.890
Is it our turn already?

00:06:22.210 --> 00:06:24.860
What makes people stronger?

00:06:24.860 --> 00:06:29.540
We may cry, shout, and fall, but we have something to believe in.

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:32.030
Because I'll leave for those who follow

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:33.950
a precedent of success!

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:35.690
A taste you can believe in.

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:36.830
I Girl Noodle.

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:40.440
That was so cool!

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:44.720
You get a commercial? No fair! No fair!

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:45.630
I didn't record this.

00:06:46.850 --> 00:06:48.640
That last cut there.

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:53.100
The shot from behind. That wasn't Chieri-san.

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:57.120
We haven't received any offers to do a commercial for I Girl Foods.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:58.060
Tsubasa-san.

00:06:58.530 --> 00:07:02.020
They just took the footage from the trial and used it.

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:04.840
Are they allowed to do that?

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:08.040
What we do is illegal in the first place.

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:12.210
Even if they use the footage without
permission, we're in no position to sue.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.870
Chieri. Return to your lane.

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:16.960
But—

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:20.420
Your fans aren't aware of the foul play involved in that commercial.

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:28.410
Chieri...

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:30.510
Why does <i>she</i> look so grumpy?

00:07:31.570 --> 00:07:34.480
If Sonata got to be in a commercial, she'd be happy.

00:07:37.730 --> 00:07:40.230
Do you think Chieri's asleep already?

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:43.440
She must be tired.

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:46.900
Her line was at least twice as long as ours.

00:07:48.490 --> 00:07:50.760
I think I'll turn in too.

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:06.240
<i>What's the deal with the Elections anyway?</i>

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:07.960
Huh?

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:09.920
Sayaka-san?

00:08:10.450 --> 00:08:11.860
This late at night?

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:15.440
Yuuko-san too.

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:19.880
<i>Until you become a star,</i>

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:25.940
<i>have the courage to never give up on your dreams.</i>

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:27.150
Working hard?

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:29.110
Takamina.

00:08:29.770 --> 00:08:33.180
Tomochin and Yukirin are practicing over there too.

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:34.610
Looks like nobody can sleep.

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:36.920
Well of course we're all antsy.

00:08:36.920 --> 00:08:38.440
It's the General Elections after all.

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:48.800
<i>That's great!</i>

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:53.760
<i>Congratulations.</i>

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:55.050
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:57.540
<i>Acchan.</i>

00:08:58.610 --> 00:09:00.160
<i>Why don't you try to cheer her up?</i>

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:05.690
<i>I doubt Hikari would feel better if I did.</i>

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:09.400
<i>Of course I wouldn't!</i>

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.900
<i>Because we're rivals!</i>

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:13.440
<i>Right.</i>

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:18.410
<i>I hope we can compete together
one day on the stage of the Elections.</i>

00:09:20.270 --> 00:09:21.520
<i>You got it!</i>

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:25.670
Acchan, you liar.

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:26.930
Yuuko...

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:29.680
I won't be satisfied with second place.

00:09:30.450 --> 00:09:33.160
I'm going to surpass Maeda Atsuko the 13th.

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:35.810
You'll have to beat me first.

00:09:35.810 --> 00:09:37.470
<i>I'm</i> going to take first place.

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:38.930
Takamina?

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:41.980
How else can I be a good role model for Kanata?

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:45.860
I'm going to stay the person she admires.

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:51.000
It's the least I could do for the girl who should have taken my place.

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:55.650
Regardless of who wins, no hard feelings, Yuuko.

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:56.660
Right.

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:58.500
I'm going to win, though.

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:09.580
Acchan.

00:10:10.530 --> 00:10:13.590
Back then, you were a star
shining far beyond my reach.

00:10:14.150 --> 00:10:16.540
But now...

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:25.890
Sensei.

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:30.250
With the Elections drawing close, the girls are all battling with their own emotions.

00:10:32.170 --> 00:10:35.570
<i>The Center Nova phenomenon that occurred with the understudies...</i>

00:10:36.170 --> 00:10:37.780
<i>With the General Elections acting as stimulus,</i>

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:39.320
<i>competition between the girls should intensify,</i>

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:42.700
<i>bringing them within a hair's
breadth of Acchan's level.</i>

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:50.350
<i>This may be the only way to solve the mystery of
the Center Novae's disappearances and save them.</i>

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:51.200
<i>Still...</i>

00:10:51.990 --> 00:10:54.380
<i>was this really the right decision?</i>

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:04.720
Sayaka-san and Yuuko-san are both working hard for the Elections.

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:06.390
I wonder why.

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:09.600
The thought of being ranked bothers me.

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:10.940
But they're...

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:13.960
Oh my.

00:11:14.910 --> 00:11:16.720
Nagisa!

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:17.920
Mimori-san.

00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:23.070
Kanata falls asleep within three seconds of crawling into bed.

00:11:24.010 --> 00:11:26.940
I didn't want to disturb her rest.

00:11:26.940 --> 00:11:28.760
Are you writing replies to fan letters?

00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:29.910
Yes.

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:33.200
Whoa. You do them all by hand?

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:34.380
That's right.

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:36.440
Can I take a look?

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:37.580
Go ahead.

00:11:39.490 --> 00:11:42.120
What they said at the handshake event and what they wore...

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:44.180
I can't believe you remembered it all.

00:11:44.610 --> 00:11:47.400
You really don't spare any effort, do you?

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:48.360
Really?

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:54.080
I'm not spending any particular effort to memorize my meetings with fans.

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:54.650
After all,

00:11:55.470 --> 00:12:00.150
I'm a fan of the people who are kind enough to be my fans.

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:02.860
A fan of your fans?

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:07.580
Although I'm never in the spotlight, they see me in the shadows

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:10.460
and shower me with their love.

00:12:10.460 --> 00:12:12.870
They say they like me.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:18.580
Sending them a reply is my way of giving them a vote of support.

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:41.110
Good morning!

00:12:42.710 --> 00:12:44.980
Makoto, you're still in your pajamas?

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:48.620
Every time we <i>finally</i> get a day off, we end up practicing anyway.

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:51.320
This time, I'm sleeping all day!

00:12:51.320 --> 00:12:53.080
All day long!

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:55.880
Sonata too!

00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:57.360
I'm gonna be lazy all day!

00:12:56.840 --> 00:12:58.460
It's cat pajamas today, huh?

00:12:57.360 --> 00:12:58.460
Catnap all day!

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:01.440
It's the day before the Elections.

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:05.220
Catnap! Catnap!

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:03.760
Should we really be relaxing?

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:05.900
It's not like it matters to us.

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:08.360
We didn't rank in the early results.

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:09.860
You're right.

00:13:09.860 --> 00:13:12.640
The whole "General Elections"
business had me worried at first,

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:15.220
but I guess if we're below tenth, it doesn't matter.

00:13:15.220 --> 00:13:17.230
You never know!

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:21.610
Everyone has an equal opportunity in the General Elections!

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:27.300
<i>Our sweat carries our dreams,</i>

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:32.000
<i>which lie budding, in wait...</i>

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:32.700
Isn't that right?

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:37.240
Well, I'm off to practice with Kanata.

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:41.600
Mimori-san has a really positive attitude.

00:13:41.600 --> 00:13:43.460
She's a hard worker, too.

00:13:45.450 --> 00:13:47.340
On second thought, I'll practice too!

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:48.510
Yeah!

00:13:48.980 --> 00:13:51.930
Sonata's gonna get elected too!

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:55.040
Come on, Grumbly. Lesson time.

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:57.980
No way! I'm gonna sleep today!

00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:01.920
All day, you hear?

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:01.920
All right. I'd better go get Chieri.

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:05.940
Chieri-san left first thing in the morning.

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:20.420
Milady.

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:25.460
A milk tea, please.

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:27.150
Certainly.

00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:29.470
It's been a while, Yasunaga.

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:33.890
I did not expect to receive a
message from you, Milady Chieri.

00:14:34.330 --> 00:14:40.540
Ever since you left home against
your father's wishes to join 0048,

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:43.620
your servant Yasunaga has been worried—

00:14:42.540 --> 00:14:44.320
The commercial for I Girl Noodle.

00:14:46.410 --> 00:14:49.920
I Girl Foods is part of the Zodiac Group.

00:14:50.590 --> 00:14:55.330
What's more, there were Zodiac cameras at the AKB trial.

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:57.200
What is the meaning of this, Yasunaga?

00:14:58.070 --> 00:15:03.670
I have a message from your
father... I mean, the CEO.

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:07.220
Chieri.

00:15:07.220 --> 00:15:09.130
I've been waiting for you, yes!

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:11.140
Father.

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:14.100
It has been a year since you left home.

00:15:14.730 --> 00:15:18.280
At first, I considered forcing you to return.

00:15:18.990 --> 00:15:23.680
But before my eyes, your radiance as an idol kept growing.

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:30.030
I am no longer opposed to
your membership in 0048.

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:36.540
I will... no, the Zodiac Group will
support you with all its resources.

00:15:37.710 --> 00:15:39.000
I knew it.

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:44.370
My solo work and that commercial
were not the results of my own skill.

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:47.460
That trial was my fault too.

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:49.050
I put everyone in danger.

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:51.760
Milady...

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:56.160
Tell my father this:

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:59.770
I refuse to let him have his way.

00:15:59.770 --> 00:16:02.770
Even if it costs me my dream!

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:06.730
Milady...

00:16:12.710 --> 00:16:14.480
Yes, come in.

00:16:16.690 --> 00:16:17.860
Chieri?

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:35.720
The rest is up to her.

00:16:39.020 --> 00:16:40.140
Welcome back!

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:43.270
Chieri, where were you?

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:47.650
We were just practicing for the mini-concert we're holding at the Elections.

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:48.860
Wanna join?

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:52.340
Sorry. I'm a bit tired.

00:16:52.340 --> 00:16:54.490
I'm in the same boat as you.

00:16:56.520 --> 00:16:58.710
I want nothing to do with the General Elections.

00:16:58.710 --> 00:16:59.410
Chieri?

00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:04.870
I don't want to bring down my friends with underhanded methods.

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:06.620
Huh?

00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:09.120
Underhanded methods?

00:17:12.270 --> 00:17:14.050
Come on, Mamoru. Hurry it up!

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:16.300
Sorry! Almost got it.

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:20.000
Darn it. Is the signal too weak or something?

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:21.310
Augh, geez!

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:23.640
The 00 General Elections are today!

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:25.270
Please work!

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:29.800
Hey, who did you vote for, Mamoru?

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:32.220
Suzuko-san, who else?

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:35.280
<i>Just</i> Suzuko?

00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:38.750
O-Of course!

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:42.780
It's fixed!

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:46.620
Awright! Kanata-san!

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:12.980
They're so cool.

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:13.920
Yeah.

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:17.860
They seem to be exuding more energy than usual.

00:18:18.610 --> 00:18:20.080
You're right.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:32.020
The Kirara are glowing as brightly as a flame.

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:32.880
Who cares about fear? Who cares about status?

00:18:32.020 --> 00:18:33.980
Perhaps it's their competitive spirit.

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:35.050
We'll stay as bold as always.

00:18:33.980 --> 00:18:35.670
Competitive spirit?

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:38.470
Are we following our dreams now?

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:41.350
With all the innocence of a child...

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:48.200
Let's break free of the chains that have held us back.

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:45.810
The last Acchan and Tsubasa-san.

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:49.420
Or rather, Mariko-sama the 7th.

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:49.070
We can't do anything.

00:18:49.070 --> 00:18:50.310
We can't do it right.

00:18:49.070 --> 00:18:50.310
chanto dekinai

00:18:49.420 --> 00:18:52.950
She was center before Acchan, after all.

00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:51.470
So what?

00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:51.470
sore ga doushita?

00:18:51.470 --> 00:18:53.350
We're still young.

00:18:51.470 --> 00:18:53.350
bokura wa wakai nda

00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:54.850
We can't do anything.

00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:54.850
nanimo dekinai

00:18:54.010 --> 00:18:56.960
Tsubasa was Center Nova too?

00:18:54.850 --> 00:18:56.350
We can't do it yet.

00:18:54.850 --> 00:18:56.350
sugu ni dekinai

00:18:56.350 --> 00:18:59.360
But that just means we're full of potential.

00:18:56.350 --> 00:18:59.360
dakara bokura ni kanousei ga aru nda

00:18:56.960 --> 00:18:58.820
No, not quite.

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:00.900
The rain has passed.

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:00.900
ame wa yanda

00:18:59.510 --> 00:19:04.330
I made center once at the Elections
before Acchan succeeded. That's all.

00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:02.360
The wind has died.

00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:02.360
kaze wa yanda

00:19:02.360 --> 00:19:03.650
A brand new light

00:19:02.360 --> 00:19:03.650
mita koto no nai

00:19:03.650 --> 00:19:05.360
is shining down.

00:19:03.650 --> 00:19:05.360
hikari ga sasu yo

00:19:04.810 --> 00:19:08.080
I didn't manage to become Center Nova, I'm afraid.

00:19:05.360 --> 00:19:06.780
Now is the time.

00:19:05.360 --> 00:19:06.780
ima ga toki da

00:19:06.280 --> 00:19:12.370
You've been reborn, Beginner!

00:19:06.280 --> 00:19:12.370
kimi wa umarekawatta Beginner!

00:19:14.350 --> 00:19:17.300
That's enough chatting for now. You're on.

00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:18.300
Right!

00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:25.510
<i>What's this?</i>

00:19:28.300 --> 00:19:29.770
<i>This energy...</i>

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:34.730
<i>The fans are acting like
they're battling for something.</i>

00:19:34.730 --> 00:19:37.620
<i>No, like they're praying.</i>

00:19:37.620 --> 00:19:38.640
<i>This is...</i>

00:19:38.640 --> 00:19:39.970
<i>...the General Elections.</i>

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:43.670
The stars that shine in the night sky

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:43.670
yoru no sora kagayaku hoshi wa

00:19:43.670 --> 00:19:46.250
lie billions of lightyears away.

00:19:43.670 --> 00:19:46.250
nanoku kounen no kanata

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:48.800
Even if the depths of despair

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:47.040
tatoe fukai zetsubou ga

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:48.800
tatoe fukai zetsubou ga

00:19:48.800 --> 00:19:51.300
should cast an endless shadow,

00:19:48.800 --> 00:19:51.300
mugen no yami to nattemo

00:19:51.300 --> 00:19:53.930
the truth will make itself heard.

00:19:51.300 --> 00:19:52.220
shinjitsu wa tsutawaru nda

00:19:52.220 --> 00:19:53.930
shinjitsu wa tsutawaru nda

00:19:53.930 --> 00:19:56.590
Who shall be the one to receive

00:19:53.930 --> 00:19:56.590
jikan no kawa ni takushita

00:19:54.550 --> 00:19:58.710
The glow from the understudies' Kirara just isn't cutting it.

00:19:56.590 --> 00:19:58.930
the message of light

00:19:56.590 --> 00:19:58.930
sono hikari no messeeji

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:00.140
Turn up the stage lights.

00:19:58.930 --> 00:20:01.350
set adrift on the river of time?

00:19:58.930 --> 00:20:01.350
uketoru mono wa dare dai?

00:20:00.140 --> 00:20:00.980
Got it.

00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:06.480
People are born, and people die.

00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:06.480
hito wa umarete hito wa shinde yuku

00:20:04.310 --> 00:20:07.220
They're overwhelmed by the atmosphere in the stadium.

00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:10.940
Our bodies don't last forever.

00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:10.940
nikutai wa horobiru yo

00:20:08.070 --> 00:20:09.830
<i>This isn't going well.</i>

00:20:09.830 --> 00:20:11.230
Girls!

00:20:11.820 --> 00:20:16.610
Those who rise back up from the ashes

00:20:11.820 --> 00:20:16.610
hai no naka kara yomigaeru mono wa

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:22.330
give passion to the next generation.

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:22.330
jounetsu tsugi no sedai he

00:20:17.560 --> 00:20:18.380
Nagisa.

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:18.940
Right!

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:25.710
Dreams are like reincarnation.

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:25.710
yume wa reincarnation

00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:30.630
I take in a sense of déjà vu

00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:30.630
nando demo deja vu no you na

00:20:29.140 --> 00:20:31.170
So they pulled it back together.

00:20:30.630 --> 00:20:32.300
with every breath.

00:20:30.630 --> 00:20:32.300
toiki wo suu

00:20:32.590 --> 00:20:36.470
It's just like reincarnation.

00:20:32.590 --> 00:20:36.470
marude reincarnation

00:20:36.470 --> 00:20:40.850
With my head still in the clouds,

00:20:36.470 --> 00:20:40.850
ima mo mata muishiki no uchi

00:20:36.640 --> 00:20:38.880
I wouldn't have it any other way.

00:20:40.850 --> 00:20:45.060
I'm running off somewhere again.

00:20:40.850 --> 00:20:45.060
dokoka e hashitteru

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:50.660
The time has finally come!

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:54.680
Welcome to the 0048 SC General Elections!

00:20:54.680 --> 00:20:59.110
I, Toku-san the 3rd, will be your MC for tonight.

00:21:04.220 --> 00:21:05.710
<i>I can feel them.</i>

00:21:05.710 --> 00:21:07.700
<i>The gazes of the fans.</i>

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:10.410
Who do you think's higher, Chieri or Nagisa?

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:20.630
Okay! We're about to announce the results

00:21:19.700 --> 00:21:20.630
That's...

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:23.290
Yes. It's to prevent tampering.

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:24.010
for the 0048 SC General Elections!

00:21:25.400 --> 00:21:27.430
Now let us begin the announcements.

00:21:36.690 --> 00:21:37.730
Here I go!

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:45.860
In tenth place, with 148,945 points,

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:49.990
75th generation understudy, Kishida Mimori!

00:21:55.980 --> 00:21:57.060
Mimori.

00:21:57.690 --> 00:21:58.620
Kanata!

00:22:05.090 --> 00:22:07.560
Wow! This is incredible!

00:22:07.560 --> 00:22:08.550
Mimori-san!

00:23:45.910 --> 00:23:47.530
Everyone looks so tense.

00:23:47.530 --> 00:23:53.180
If we make it onto that stage,
we can also return our fans' love.

00:23:53.180 --> 00:23:55.530
I didn't earn those votes!

00:23:56.290 --> 00:23:59.340
Now let us begin the announcements.

00:23:57.580 --> 00:24:00.040
- The New General Elections-
